GTK mixed-link test 5: Geany and L3afpad sharing one GTK
=======================================================

A TEST, not a release (riscos-gtk + riscos-crossdev 1.11-test1).

Geany and L3afpad are linked "mixed": UnixLib is inside each program, as
usual, but GTK 3.24.52, riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend and the libraries
under them (GLib, cairo, pango, harfbuzz, FreeType, fontconfig, pixman,
libpng, libjpeg...) are 26 shared libraries in !GTKLibs, loaded by
!SharedLibs (SOManager and ld-riscos/so/2). Every mixed GTK program uses
the same !GTKLibs, so with several running there is one copy of GTK in
memory (test 2 on a Pi: 20 MB with Geany and L3afpad both open).

Sizes of the programs themselves:
  Geany    6.7 MB  (22.6 MB static, RC17)
  L3afpad  0.75 MB (17.2 MB static, RC17)
  !GTKLibs 20.5 MB, shared by every mixed GTK program

!GTKLibs, like !SharedLibs, lives in !Boot.Resources. PackMan will install
it there; for this test it comes in its own zip (GTKLibs-3.24.52-18.zip).

You need
--------
- RISC OS 5 on ARMv7 or later (Pi 2 or later), 16 or 32 bpp mode
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, ARMEABISupport and Iconv (PackMan),
  as for the normal GTK programs
- !SharedLibs in !Boot.Resources, a version with ld-riscos/so/2 (GCCSDK 8
  or later, as Iris's is). The older !SharedLibs 4.0 from riscos.info has
  only ld-riscos/so/1 and can't run these; each !Run says so.
- !GTKLibs in !Boot.Resources (from GTKLibs-3.24.52-18.zip)

Trying it
---------
1. Copy Resources.!GTKLibs from GTKLibs-3.24.52-18.zip into !Boot.Resources
   (shift-double-click !Boot to open it, then Resources). Replace any
   earlier !GTKLibs.
2. Restart (or just double-click !Geany: its !Run boots !GTKLibs and
   !SharedLibs from !Boot.Resources if they haven't been yet).
3. Run !MemReport: the "before" figures.
4. Double-click !Geany. When its window is open, run !MemReport again.
5. Double-click !L3afpad. When its window is open, run !MemReport again.

!MemReport writes <Wimp$ScrapDir>.MemReport and opens it (each run
replaces it, so copy each one before the next).

What to look at
---------------
- "Shared Libraries" (SOManager's dynamic area): about 20 MB after
  Geany starts, and still about 20 MB with L3afpad open too.
- Each program's slot ("geany:", "l3afpad:").
- For comparison, the same with the normal RC17 Geany and L3afpad
  (static): their slots, with both open.
- Each program's Log, <Wimp$ScrapDir>.Geany.Log and .L3afpad.Log: the
  "riscos-gtk: started: ... ready after N s" line.

Files
-----
GTKMixed-test5.zip:
  !Geany        Geany 2.1, mixed (geany,e1f is the ELF program)
  !L3afpad      L3afpad 0.8.18.1.11, mixed (l3afpad,e1f)
  !MemReport    writes the memory report described above
GTKLibs-3.24.52-18.zip:
  Resources.!GTKLibs   the 26 shared libraries, for !Boot.Resources

